{% extends 'layout/shell.twig' %}

{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE ORGANISATION CONSOLE FRAME — every section of /org
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Destroyed 3 Oct 2026 with the rest of the public pages (inventory
  pages--org--dashboard.md) and rebuilt here. `GET /org` has been routed to a template that
  does not exist ever since, so the console an organisation manages its money from has been
  a 500 — which is why nothing on it resembled the design: there was no page.

  ── IT IS THE ACCOUNT CONSOLE'S FRAME, DELIBERATELY ─────────────────────────

  `pages/account/_frame.twig` already solved this screen: a rail of sections beside a
  content column from 600 up, no rail at all on a phone, and EVERY SECTION AN ADDRESS
  (`?tab=`) so the phone's pushed screens and the desktop's rail are the same pages
  (REFERENCE §7.2). Inventing a second console pattern would mean two answers to "how does
  a signed-in area navigate here", and the one that gets maintained is whichever a
  contributor opened first. Same markup names (`acx-*`), same rail, same app bar.

  What is NOT shared is the gate: which sections an organisation is offered depends on what
  it is, and that answer lives in `Services\OrgRail::offers()` — asked by the rail AND by
  each section, so a tab can never lead to a section that refuses to draw.

  A child sets, at template scope (a set inside a block is invisible to the others):
    org_tab   the section key (Services\OrgRail::SECTIONS)
    rail      OrgRail::tabs(), from the controller
  and fills `org_body`.
#}

{% set _tab   = org_tab|default('overview') %}
{% set _title = org_title(_tab) %}
{% set _lead  = org_lead(_tab) %}
{% set app_bar = app_bar|default({variant: 'child', title: _title, back: _tab == 'overview' ? '/' : '/org', share: false}) %}
{% set colour_tier = colour_tier|default('2') %}

{% block head_styles %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/account.css') }}"><link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/org.css') }}">{% block org_styles %}{% endblock %}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="acx">
  <aside class="acx-rail" aria-label="{{ 'Your organisation'|trans }}">
    {#
      WHO THIS CONSOLE IS LOOKING AT, AND WHAT IT IS ALLOWED TO CLAIM.

      The design draws "Verified organisation" under the name. Printed as a constant it says
      that beside a SUSPENDED account — on the console whose first panel exists to explain
      the suspension. It is derived from the status, and the second line of the signed-in
      person is their role, because "view only" changes what every button below will do.
    #}
    <div class="acx-rail__who">
      <span class="org-mono" aria-hidden="true">{{ org.name|slice(0, 1)|upper }}</span>
      <span class="acx-rail__id">
        <b>{{ org.name }}</b>
        <span>{{ org_standing }}</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <nav class="acx-rail__nav" aria-label="{{ 'Sections'|trans }}">
      {% for t in rail|default([]) %}
        <a class="acx-tab" href="{{ t.href }}"{% if t.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <span class="acx-ico acx-ico--{{ t.tone }}" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="{{ t.d }}"/></svg></span>
          <span class="acx-tab__l">{{ t.label }}</span>
          {% if t.n %}<span class="acx-n{{ t.attention ? ' acx-n--on' }}">{{ t.n }}</span>{% endif %}
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>
    <div class="org-rail__foot">
      <p class="org-rail__me">{{ me.name|default(me.email) }}<span>{{ org_role }}</span></p>
      <form method="post" action="/org/logout">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
        <button class="org-out" type="submit">{{ 'Sign out'|trans }}</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <div class="acx-main">
    <div class="acx-title">
      <h1 class="acx-title__h">{{ _title }}</h1>
      {% if _lead %}<p class="acx-title__p">{{ _lead }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if _lead %}<p class="acx-lead-ph">{{ _lead }}</p>{% endif %}

    {#
      THE CAVEAT THAT HAS TO BE ABOVE THE BUTTONS IT GOVERNS.

      "View only" changes what every form on every section will do, so it belongs in the
      reading order before them — not in a rail somebody has already scrolled past on a
      phone, where there is no rail at all.
    #}
    {% if me.role != 'owner' %}
      <p class="org-note" role="note">{{ 'You have view-only access, so you cannot upload a document, accept an offer, edit your page or move money.'|trans }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if flash_ok %}<p class="org-flag org-flag--ok" role="status">{{ flash_ok }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if flash_error %}<p class="org-flag org-flag--err" role="alert">{{ flash_error }}</p>{% endif %}

    {% block org_body %}{% endblock %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
